Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> I generally agree with what you say, but I'd be interested what people
> think about intrinsics timing out after, say, 20000 moves.

Nethack+ worked like that: to gain an intrinsic permanently from
eating, it had to be acquired twice.  The first granted it only
temporarily, then it had to be effectively gained again before the
first expired to get it for good.  I remember thinking that the
expiration period was too short (far less than 20k moves), and it was
of the reasons I stopped playing that version, but I think the idea is
interesting in principle.

The game can be won in 20,000 moves if a player sprints through the
dungeons, so it's certainly not too short.  That's about the number of
turns it takes for a reading of a spellbook to run out, and usually my
own books don't need to be reread more than once in a game unless I'm
dawdling.  It might be so long that it wouldn't play enough of a role
in the game, but it also means that a careless player might have a
major intrinsic expire at the wrong moment.

Another possibility is to implement multiple levels of intrinsics,
which is a staple of the Moria/Angband line of roguelikes and was also
part of a recent patch seen hereabouts....

